    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "line": 55,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "### Sub-Agent Protocol"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "line": 57,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "Every sub-agent extends one base class with a single abstract `run(context) -> Result`,"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "line": 100,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "never learns the sub-agent exists."
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "line": 121,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "## 4. Sub-Agent Retry and Validation"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "line": 123,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "Wrap every sub-agent call in retry **and** validation, and keep the two apart: a call that"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "line": 271,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "**A sub-agent's value is its own window**: it returns a typed summary, not a"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/context-engineering.md",
    "line": 26,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "- Sub-agent context isolation"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/context-engineering.md",
    "line": 162,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "## Sub-agent context isolation"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/context-engineering.md",
    "line": 164,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "A sub-agent's value is not that it is a different prompt. **It is that it has its own"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/context-engineering.md",
    "line": 167,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "The contract: the sub-agent receives a task and the context it needs, works in a window"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/context-engineering.md",
    "line": 172,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "costs the parent one paragraph. It also sets the design rule \u2014 if a sub-agent's return"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/governance.md",
    "line": 36,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "The last one is the one most designs miss: a sub-agent that inherits its caller's"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/governance.md",
    "line": 51,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "rather than the first. Sub-agent isolation comes from exactly two mechanisms used together:"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/governance.md",
    "line": 54,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "sub-agent handed its parent's transcript has been told about every capability you carefully"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/graph-engineering.md",
    "line": 66,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "same subagent may own several nodes, and a node owned by a person is still a node. The"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/graph-engineering.md",
    "line": 345,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "| `agent(prompt, opts)` | one subagent | `opts.schema` forces a validated object back, so downstream stages get data, not prose to parse |"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/patterns.md",
    "line": 15,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "- [Sub-agent retry, and the error hierarchy under it](#sub-agent-retry-and-the-error-hierarchy-under-it)"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/patterns.md",
    "line": 203,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "## The orchestrator's shared context and sub-agent protocol"
  },
  {
    "member": "agent-stack",
    "skill": "agent-orchestrator",
    "path": "plugins/agent-stack/skills/agent-orchestrator/references/patterns.md",
    "line": 244,
    "kind": "delegation",
    "text": "The single abstract method is what keeps the orchestrator ignorant of any sub-agent's"
